  VALUES ('CORE', 181, 'Live data layer: Pinia Colada, patient card as the pattern', 'Cross-view refresh relies on hand-written window events (patient-changed, checklist-updated). Any screen nobody wired up stays stale until F5, and every visit to a view refetches behind a spinner.', 'Add Pinia Colada as the query layer: data lives under keys (`[''patient'', id]`) and a mutation invalidates those keys. Move the patient card first as the reference pattern, with optimistic save. Live push from the API (SSE) is a separate follow-up ticket (decision D3 = "more").',
    '* Saving a visit refreshes the patient list, the calendar and the patient card without F5 (e2e test).
* Returning to the patient card shows cached data immediately and revalidates in the background (test).
* A failed optimistic save rolls back and shows the error (test).
* The patient card uses no window events; a short ADR documents the pattern for the other views.

Decision: [https://claude.ai/artifact/7d4M9s7oxnkVjbLgz6PhVG](<https://claude.ai/artifact/7d4M9s7oxnkVjbLgz6PhVG>)', 'backlog', 2, '{}'::text[],
